# Mobile app environment variables.
#
# IMPORTANT: Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are readable by the app, and every
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is bundled into the client JavaScript. NEVER put secrets
# (API keys, Django SECRET_KEY, database URLs, AWS/service-role credentials)
# in this file — those belong on the backend only.

# Base URL of the Django API the app talks to (used for auth + submissions).
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for normal local development (you usually don't need a
# `.env` at all). When unset, the app derives the API host from the Metro dev
# server (http://<your-LAN-ip>:8000) so a physical device reaches your machine
# rather than itself — remember `localhost` on a phone is the phone. Run Django
# with `python manage.py runserver 0.0.0.0:8000` and keep the phone on the same
# LAN. The app logs the resolved URL on startup in dev: `[api] base URL: …`.
#
# Set it explicitly only when the derived host is wrong (Expo tunnel mode, a
# deployed backend, or WSL2 port-forwarding setups) — and then to a URL that
# actually resolves. Setting a placeholder here silently breaks every API call.
# See docs/troubleshooting.md → "The app can't reach the backend".
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8000
